{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"13241075","self":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/13241075","key":"KAFKA-8587","fields":{"summary":"One producer per thread for Kafka Streams EOS","resolutiondate":"2020-05-05T05:55:55.705+0000","created":"2019-06-23T03:30:46.526+0000","description":"Currently exactly-once producer is coupled with individual input partitions. This is not a well scaled solution for client application such as Kafka Streams, and the root cause is that EOS producer doesn't understand the topic partition move throughout consumer group rebalance. By amending this semantic gap, we could achieve much better EOS scalability.","issuelinks":[],"comment":{"comments":[],"maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"status":{"self":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/status/5","description":"A resolution has been taken, and it is awaiting verification by reporter. From here issues are either reopened, or are closed.","iconUrl":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/resolved.png","name":"Resolved","id":"5","statusCategory":{"self":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/statuscategory/3","id":3,"key":"done","colorName":"green","name":"Done"}}},"renderedFields":{"summary":null,"resolutiondate":"05/May/20 05:55","created":"23/Jun/19 03:30","description":"<p>Currently exactly-once producer is coupled with individual input partitions. This is not a well scaled solution for client application such as Kafka Streams, and the root cause is that EOS producer doesn't understand the topic partition move throughout consumer group rebalance. By amending this semantic gap, we could achieve much better EOS scalability.</p>","issuelinks":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"status":null}}